# What a reviewer sees first.
#
# Markdown here is mostly not prose somebody wrote for this change. records/ is
# rendered from the store by `make export`, so a diff of it is a diff of a
# rendering — the reviewable form of records whose source of truth is the
# insert-only log. In one recent change it was 487 lines against 47 of
# hand-written prose and 1,329 of code, and it is the first thing a reviewer
# scrolls past.
#
# `linguist-generated=true` collapses a file in the pull request diff. It is
# hidden by default and expanded with one click; nothing is removed, and the
# file is still committed, still exported, still checked by `make check`. It
# also drops these files from the repository's language statistics, which is
# the more honest figure for a tree whose code is Go.
#
# Two are exempt, because they are how somebody arriving works out what this is
# ([MUS-D-0136](records/decisions.md#mus-d-0136)). Later rules win, so the
# exemptions follow the rule they carve out of.
*.md            linguist-generated=true
/CLAUDE.md      linguist-generated=false
/README.md      linguist-generated=false
